diff --git a/Documentation/security/keys/trusted-encrypted.rst b/Documentation/security/keys/trusted-encrypted.rst
index f4d7e162d5e4..b20ebfaf811e 100644
--- a/Documentation/security/keys/trusted-encrypted.rst
+++ b/Documentation/security/keys/trusted-encrypted.rst
@@ -50,6 +50,15 @@ safe.
          and the UNIQUE key. Default is to use the UNIQUE key, but selecting
          the OTP key can be done via a module parameter (dcp_use_otp_key).
 
+     (5) RPi firmware crypto (Raspberry Pi VideoCore firmware OTP-backed HMAC)
+
+         Rooted to a device-unique key stored in on-chip OTP fuses and
+         accessible only to the VideoCore firmware. The kernel requests
+         HMAC-SHA256(otp_key, nonce) over the firmware mailbox and the raw OTP
+         key material never leaves the firmware. The resulting HMAC output is
+         used as an AES-256-GCM wrapping key making sealed blobs
+         device-specific and non-migratable.
+
   *  Execution isolation
 
      (1) TPM
@@ -71,6 +80,13 @@ safe.
          environment. Only basic blob key encryption is executed there.
          The actual key sealing/unsealing is done on main processor/kernel space.
 
+     (5) RPi firmware crypto
+
+         Crypto operations execute inside the VideoCore firmware which runs
+         in a separate processing domain from the Arm application cores.
+         The OTP key is readable only by firmware code not by the kernel
+         directly.
+
   * Optional binding to platform integrity state
 
      (1) TPM
@@ -98,6 +114,13 @@ safe.
          Relies on Secure/Trusted boot process (called HAB by vendor) for
          platform integrity.
 
+     (5) RPi firmware crypto
+
+         No boot-state binding is provided (no PCR equivalent). A sealed blob
+         will unseal on any boot of the same physical device as long as the OTP
+         key slot has not been revoked.Platform integrity must therefore be
+         established through other means (e.g. secure boot chain).
+
   *  Interfaces and APIs
 
      (1) TPM
@@ -118,6 +141,13 @@ safe.
          Vendor-specific API that is implemented as part of the DCP crypto driver in
          ``drivers/crypto/mxs-dcp.c``.
 
+     (5) RPi firmware crypto
+
+         Interface is the Raspberry Pi VideoCore firmware mailbox property
+         protocol (``include/soc/bcm2835/raspberrypi-firmware.h``). The
+         crypto tags used (``0x0003008f``, ``0x00030092``) require a firmware
+         build that includes OTP crypto support.
+
   *  Threat model
 
      The strength and appropriateness of a particular trust source for a given
@@ -160,6 +190,10 @@ selected trust source:
      a dedicated hardware RNG that is independent from DCP which can be enabled
      to back the kernel RNG.
 
+  *  RPi firmware crypto: Kernel RNG
+
+     The normal kernel random number generator is used to generate keys.
+
 Users may override this by specifying ``trusted.rng=kernel`` on the kernel
 command-line to override the used RNG with the kernel's random number pool.
 
@@ -275,6 +309,29 @@ Usage::
 specific to this DCP key-blob implementation.  The key length for new keys is
 always in bytes. Trusted Keys can be 32 - 128 bytes (256 - 1024 bits).
 
+Trusted Keys usage: RPi firmware crypto
+----------------------------------------
+
+Prerequisites:
+
+* A Raspberry Pi SoC with VideoCore firmware that supports the OTP crypto
+  mailbox tags (``0x0003008f`` / ``0x00030092``).
+* The target OTP key slot must be programmed (non-zero) before use.
+  A slot with all-zero content causes the firmware to return an error.
+
+Key slot 1 is used by default. Override with ``trusted.rpifwcrypto_key_id=N``
+if a different slot is needed.
+
+Usage::
+
+    keyctl add trusted name "new keylen" ring
+    keyctl add trusted name "load hex_blob" ring
+    keyctl print keyid
+
+"keyctl print" returns an ASCII hex copy of the sealed key, which is in format
+specific to this rpifwcrypto key-blob implementation. The key length for new keys is
+always in bytes. Trusted Keys can be 32 - 128 bytes (256 - 1024 bits).
+
 Encrypted Keys usage
 --------------------
 
